## In Progress



## Open

- [ ] **ADRs / decision records.** Establish where architecture decisions are recorded. Today
  they are scattered across `designs/DESIGN-*.md` and `plans/PLAN-*.md` with no dedicated ADR
  location or index. Decide on a home (e.g. `docs/adr/NNNN-*.md`) and format, then have an agent
  walk the complete conversation/message history and back-fill ADRs for decisions made there that
  aren't yet captured in a design/plan. Keep them topic-neutral — do not reference the original
  source-document subject matter in any ADR.

- [ ] All plans in the `plans/`
- [ ] title and source_path should be in metadata, probably. filename on the other side is not providing value given source_path exists and can be dropped. source_id and source_hash should move to Document. their calculation should be handled by a user-provided function (passed down from Parser/ Pipeline) that takes the path only. Default should be the path as str for id and a sha-256 of the file for the hash. This way we can have consistent provenance across parsers and also allow users to inject custom logic (e.g. include content-based hash of the document, or use a different stable id source like a database record id). This is relevant for the vector store sync/update logic to determine what has changed.
Also, per default the whole metadata should be included in render_for_prompt.
- [ ] For BaseMetadata when dumping to json - which is used for self-query-retrieval mostly - think about annotating the fields with something like description as in pydantic Field. Maybe switch to pydantic?
- [ ] Split guide/ into "*using" and "*build_your_own" per module. e.g. splitting.md and build_splitter.md, rendering.md and build_renderer.md, etc. The "using" guides are for users who just want to use the library with built-in components; the "build_your_own" guides are for users who want to implement custom parsers, processors, renderers, etc. This separation keeps the basic usage guides concise and approachable while still providing detailed instructions for advanced customization.
- [ ] Think about logging. maybe use loguru. should already be an indirect dependency.
- [ ] documentation searchable for llms: https://github.com/mensfeld/llm-docs-builder

- [ ] Add pdf parser PaddleOCR-VL which is ranked 1st at https://opendatalab.com/omnidocbench https://github.com/PADDLEPADDLE/PADDLEOCR

- [ ] Add https://github.com/opendataloader-project/opendataloader-pdf

- [ ] Benchmarking (see PLAN_BENCHMARKING_PARSING.md): 
