### Low-priority:

- [ ] **UpdateResult: distinguish skip reasons.** `VectorStorePipeline.UpdateResult.skipped` currently conflates "hash unchanged (ProvenanceProcessor returned None)" with "dropped by any other DocumentProcessor returning None". To separate these, the pipeline's return type would need a structured skip reason. See `DESIGN_VECTORSTORE_DECOMPOSITION.md` — Known limitation section.

- [ ] Example of how to build a custom graph-rag from the outputs (events (time_relevant_from, time_relevant_to), entities (person, organisation, location, facility, ...), sources, relationships between entities (visits, )). Idea would be to be able to extract a flat timeline with filters for entity types, time ranges, etc.

- [ ] Review the use of bounding boxes: https://medium.com/@michael71314/how-to-use-ocr-bounding-boxes-c00303bc11c4

- [ ]Custom Parser Extension Points: Extend `from_path()` with a user-configurable extension registry so users can register
  custom file extensions without modifying library code. `from_path()` should check the registry
  before the built-in `match`, so user-registered extensions take precedence. (`parsing/__init__.py`)

  ```python
  _extension_registry: dict[str, Callable[[Path], DocumentSource]] = {}

  def register_extension(ext: str, factory: Callable[[Path], DocumentSource]) -> None:
      _extension_registry[ext.lower()] = factory
  ```

- [ ] Make `DocumentSource` a structural `Protocol` instead of a closed `Union` to remove
  type errors when passing user-defined sources to `load_document()`. Runtime behaviour is
  unchanged — `load_file` is already open via singledispatch. (`parsing/__init__.py`)

---

#### HTML Parser fixes

- [ ] Fix the h>6 heading hack in `parsing/html/load.py`: the current workaround searches for
  `<p class="heading">` tags to handle `<hN>` where N > 6 that pandoc may emit. This is
  fragile — replace with a proper normalization step that rewrites out-of-range heading tags
  to `<h6>` before parsing. (`parsing/html/load.py:171`)

- [ ] Add a test case for `<p class="heading">` / h>6 heading parsing in the HTML parser test
  suite. (`parsing/html/load.py:174`)

- [ ] Improve heading section extraction: `_extract_heading_sections()` iterates all siblings
  linearly; a cleaner approach is to find all headings first, then walk siblings between
  consecutive headings. Also evaluate whether bare `<p>` tags before a heading (without
  `class="heading"`) should be included or filtered. (`parsing/html/load.py:184`,
  `parsing/html/load.py:178`)

- [ ] Add logging on `requests.exceptions.ConnectionError` in the HTML image downloader
  instead of silently returning `None`. (`parsing/html/load.py:110`)

