## Done


- [x] think about removing render_for_embedding. The creation of embedding content is actually taken over by chunker now. (Done: removed render_for_embedding, BaseElement.summary, TableSummaryProcessor. Merged Image.summary into text_representation. Added decorative image skip logic.)
- [x] Get rid of position marker — order is preserved in the list of elements.
- [x] All BaseElements should have an html-interface: html property and html setter. It could
  just be a passthrough to html_text or _html, but the setter should extract all the
  element-specific information like alt text, width/height for images, etc.; level of headings.
  This way we can easily convert any element to html and back without losing information.
- [x] Create specialized BaseElement-renderers for prompt-content, embedding-content and
  raw-data. All implemented via singledispatch with register/unregister functionality to swap
  out the rendering logic for specific types easily.
  (render_for_prompt, render_for_embedding, render_raw in rendering/elements.py)
- [x] Delete RIXML parser and `test_rixml.py` — file is entirely commented out; RIXML parser tests should be re-written from scratch when the parser is re-integrated.
- [x] Rename `test_footnote_processing.py` → `test_processing_footnote.py` to match
  `src/ragdoc/processing/footnote.py`.
- [x] Split `test_summary_processors.py` into one file per source module:
  `test_processing_summary_base.py`, `test_processing_summary_image.py`,
  `test_processing_summary_table.py`, `test_processing_summary_document.py`.
- [x] Split `test_rendering.py` into `test_rendering_base.py`, `test_rendering_elements.py`,
  and `test_rendering.py` (TestRenderer only).
- [x] Merge `test_html_preface.py` (single test) into `test_html.py`, then delete the file.
- [x] Merge `test_nested_images.py` (single test) into `test_pandoc.py`, then delete the file.
- [x] Delete `test_aa_document_processing.py` — redundant importability test.


- [x] Create DocumentProcessor for footnotes with extendable pattern matching for generating
  FootnoteCandidates from elements.html. And easily swappable heuristic-generation logic for
  ranking FootnoteCandidates. Current Ideas would be to use the surrounding text (commas,
  sentence-ends, word-ends etc should increase likelihood in different amounts) and the
  position of other footnotes (based on numbering) should be able to influence each footnote
  candidates score as well.
  Note: FootnoteProcessor, FootnoteCandidate, FootnoteResolver protocol, SimpleFootnoteResolver
  and LLMFootnoteResolver are all implemented in processing/footnote.py. The resolver strategy
  is already injectable. What remains is making the candidate-generation step pluggable (currently
  find_footnote_candidates() is a standalone function, not swappable) and adding symbol-based
  pattern matching alongside the existing number-based \b{number}\b pattern.

- [x] HTML footnote parsing — detect anchor-link footnotes within the page (i.e. `<a href="#footnote-N">[N]</a>`
  in body text, resolved to `<p id="footnote-N">...</p>` at page bottom). Add tests for:
  - HTML with `<a href="#...">` in-page links as produced by pandoc or browser renders
  - Markdown with pandoc-style in-document links (e.g. `[text][^ref]` converted to HTML anchors)
  - Native pandoc markdown footnote syntax:
    ```
    Here is a footnote reference,[^1] and another.[^longnote]

    [^1]: Here is the footnote.

    [^longnote]: Here's one with multiple blocks.

        Subsequent paragraphs are indented to show that they
    belong to the previous footnote.

            { some.code }
    ```
  Decide whether each footnote extraction strategy (anchor-link detection, pandoc markdown) should
  be implemented as a `TSoupTransformer` (preprocessing step inside the HTML parser) or as a
  `SyncDocumentProcessor` (post-parse stage). If soup transformer is the right fit, register it as
  a default transformer in the HTML parser pipeline. Existing xfail tests in
  `tests/parsing/test_html_anchor_footnotes.py` cover part of this.


- [x] See PLAN_TEST_ROUNDTRIP.md: Think about a clean way to replace image-inline links with image data when rendering.
  Maybe pass the baseelement-renderer to a document-renderer and this handles images + footnotes?
  Note: The Renderer already resolves <ref id='...'/> placeholders via _resolve_inline_refs(),
  so the rendering side is clean. The right pattern for embedding image data is a pre-render
  DocumentProcessor that downloads remote URLs and stores base64 data on Image elements — not
  logic inside the renderer itself. The Renderer then just calls render_raw/render_for_prompt
  on the Image element, which can emit an <img src="data:..."> tag if data is present.

- [x] See PLAN_PIPELINE.md: think about "multiple embeddings for one content" pattern. In the simple case, we let the user handle it. the question is how far we should go into the vector db interface anyways.
But it might be really helpful to have a Document- summarizer generate a list of summaries per perceived topic (for retrieval purposes). Question is: should that produce one chunk (where somehow we have to solve that the embedding is calculated for each summary) or multiple chunks (where deduplication of content is handled by user later on)? 
Actually, based on this writing, its pretty clear it should be multiple chunks.
New Question: which thing should be responsible to create those multiple chunks from one document? Probably a different Chunker.
This would mean: the Document-Summarizer becomes part of a "SimpleChunker", document doesnt need a summary field anymore and another "LLMChunker" would be responsible to call an LLM summarizer and create multiple summaries for a given document-content.

- [x] [BIG FEATURE] merging: See PLAN_MERGE_HTML_PARITY.md Smart document merging across different parsers (mineru, azure_di, docx).